<title>TURKEY: Turkish Brisa 96 net profits up 177 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Brisa 96 net profits up 177 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	6,424.16 vs   2,322.61</p>
<p>    Net profit			 6,829.68 vs   2,469.22</p>
<p>    Net sales			 24,571.05 vs  12,782.93</p>
<p>    Operating profit		 8,597.12 vs   3,795.41</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	     2,444.70 vs     568.54</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense		581.15 vs     516.64</p>
<p>    Interest paid			 34.00 vs	57.20</p>
<p>    Total debts			7,065.33 vs   4,200.83</p>
<p>    Equity			    16,217.70 vs   7,761.50</p>
<p>    Capital			    1,063.13 vs   1,063.13</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's tyre producer Brisa Bridgestone Sabanci Lastik Sanayi ve Ticaret A.S. is owned jointly by Japan's Bridgestone Corp and companies of Turkish industrial and financial conglomerate Sabanci Holding.</p>
<p>Figures do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
